SUMMARY:Toronto Summer Music Festival:  Two Sides Of The Same Fiddle   
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n**Let's explore how discipline and del
 ight share the same four strings\, and what truly separates a violin from 
 a fiddle!**\n\nYou could use the 10% off promo code for tickets ($40-$80)\
 n\nTicket link is below...\n\nWilliam Fedkenheuer\, violin\nOrion Weiss\, 
 piano\nBen Plotnick\, fiddle\nEric Wright\, cello\n\n**Program:**\n\nBeeth
 oven: Violin Sonata No. 8 in G Major\, Op. 30\, No. 3\n\nDvořák: Sonatin
 a in G Major for Violin and Piano\, Op. 100\, B. 183\n\n*Additional fiddle
  tunes to follow\, to be announced from the stage.*\n\n\\*\\*\\*From sonat
 a to stomp\, Artistic Director William Fedkenheuer moves between classical
  refinement with Orion Weiss and the rhythmic spark of country traditions 
 alongside Ben Plotnick and Eric Wright of The Fretless — exploring how d
 iscipline and delight share the same four strings\, and what truly separat
 es a violin from a fiddle.\n\n**Ticket link and seating chart:**\n\n**Use 
 promo code** CULTURE10 (for 10% off)\n\nhttps://torontosummermusic.com/eve
 nt/two-sides-of-the-same-fiddle/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31558
 8894/
